abstract: >-
  Research software and supplementary data for a computational M-3 mine-to-mill
  simulation study. Includes a deterministic synthetic-profile generator,
  research simulation engine v3, scenario catalogue, PPO checkpoints, batch
  runner, software tests and confirmatory statistical-analysis scripts. The
  archived outputs cover two experiments with 24 scenarios and 300 replications
  per scenario: 57,600 result rows for E1 and 72,000 for E2. Input profiles are
  synthetic reconstructions based on manuscript equations, assumptions and
  seeds; they are not recovered historical records or field measurements.
  Results are simulation estimates, not observed operational savings. The SAG
  energy equation is not calibrated with plant data, and no crusher transfer
  function is implemented. The separate Constancia aggregate analysis does
  not calibrate or validate the M-3 model.
